course: dictionary
lesson: 7271
title: Pimple: a small spot or bump
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A pimple is a small red spot on the skin, sometimes with yellow pus in the middle. Teenagers often get pimples as they grow up, because their skin makes more oil.
explain: Read the words around a new word to find its meaning. Health lessons say to wash gently and not squeeze pimples, so the clues show it is a spot on your skin that needs care.
explain: The word also appears in «goose pimples». Here the pimples are the little bumps that rise on your skin when you are cold or scared, not spots. Context tells you which meaning fits.
explain: In the story, the goloshes (rubber boots) had «pimples on their soles». These are small raised bumps pressed into the rubber, so the tracks they left were easy to read.
fact: A pimple is a small red spot on the skin.
fact: Some pimples have yellow pus in the middle.
fact: «Goose pimples» are the small bumps on your skin when you feel cold or scared.
fact: In the story, «pimples» are small raised bumps on the soles of new goloshes, which leave clear tracks.
fact: Pimple is a noun, and its plural is pimples.
exercise: What is a pimple? | *A small red spot on the skin | A kind of bird that lives in the wood | A large bruise from a fall | Dirt that washes off in the bath
exercise: «Goose pimples» are what? | *Little bumps on the skin when you feel cold or scared | Feathers that grow on a goose | A kind of rain that falls in winter | A red spot that hurts when touched
exercise: Copy the word from «The goloshes were new, just bought for the winter, and the pimples on their soles were fresh and sharp» that means small raised bumps. | winter | goloshes | *pimples | sharp
test: Why do teenagers often get pimples? | They have eaten too many carrots | They have been out in the sun all day | They have caught a cold | *Their skin makes more oil
test: What does health advice say to do about pimples? | Cover them with a thick layer of mud | Pop them as often as you can | *Wash gently and do not squeeze them | Squeeze them hard every morning
exam: In «Mia has a pimple on her chin», what does pimple mean? | *A small red spot on the skin | A big yellow bird | A type of heavy rain | A loud noise from the kitchen
